📗
  🏥 The diagnostic app. Its routes report what the server saw and produce
  awkward responses on demand, so tests can check the engine from outside.

    /                      text "ok"
    /inspect[/:value]      GET POST PUT PATCH DELETE: one fact per line
    POST /bytes            the request body, byte for byte
    POST /json             the request body read as JSON and written back, or a 400 that says why it is not JSON
    /stream/:count         that many chunks, streamed; ?delay=ms waits before each later chunk
    /eight/:a/…/:h         its eight parameters, joined with commas
    /items                 puts eight items in the request's bag and reads them back
    /id                    the request's ID, as the handler sees it
    /own-id                an answer that brings an X-Request-Id of its own
    /status/:code          that status, with the body "body"
    /header?value=…        puts the value in an X-Echo response header
    /framing               sets the headers that only the server may set
    /stop                  asks the server to stop, then answers
    /slow/:ms              answers after that many milliseconds
    /raise/problem         raises a 404 problem with a message for a field
    /raise/plain           raises an error that carries no problem
    POST /raise/late       reads the body as JSON, then raises: a 422 if it was JSON
    /raise/again           catches what something it called raised, and raises it again
